cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these visualizations, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Interactive visualizations for computer networks courses"
abstract: >-
  Self-contained, interactive HTML visualizations for teaching computer
  networks at undergraduate level: line coding and bit time, transmission and
  propagation delays, space-time and timing diagrams, layering and
  encapsulation, queueing and packet drops in a router, DNS names, zone
  delegation and query resolution, and persistent HTTP with and without
  pipelining. Every visualization is one HTML file with no dependencies that
  works offline, and is available in Spanish and English. Developed for the
  course Network Architecture I (Arquitectura de Redes I) at the University of
  Alcalá, Spain.
